      "text": "50-year-old male presenting with excessive thirst and frequent urination for 2 months. Character: passing urine many times, also at night; radiation: n/a; aggravated by sweet food; relieved by nothing. Severity 7/10. Associated: tiredness, blurred vision, weight loss. PMH: Type 2 diabetes for 5 years; Appendectomy in 1998. Drugs: Metformin 500 mg. Allergy: no known allergies. Family: diabetes. Personal: non-smoker, no alcohol. Triage: ROUTINE."
